       - Use DID in any revenue-generating context without permission

    d) Derivative Work Restrictions
       - Create derivative works for public distribution
       - Publish modified versions of the DID package
       - Share modifications with external parties without permission
       - Use DID as the basis for a competing skill or product
       - Sublicense or redistribute derivative works
       - Create open-source versions of DID components

    e) Distribution Restrictions
       - Share the DID package with unauthorized parties
       - Upload to public repositories without permission
       - Distribute via package managers without authorization
       - Mirror or host the DID package externally
       - Create copies for distribution to third parties
       - Share access credentials or installation files

    f) Intellectual Property Violations
       - Disclose trade secrets or proprietary methodologies
       - Reverse engineer the DID package
